1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:40,364 --> 00:01:40,964
Your F.D.A.

8
00:01:41,144 --> 00:01:46,684
Is Unsafe and Ineffective A drug passes every safety test your species invented.

9
00:01:47,084 --> 00:01:47,864
It won't hurt you.

10
00:01:48,464 --> 00:01:49,224
Everyone agrees.

11
00:01:49,744 --> 00:01:53,004
You still can't have it for another eight point two years.

12
00:01:53,624 --> 00:01:56,043
There is, however, no waiting list for dying.

13
00:01:56,264 --> 00:01:57,104
No one blocks that.

14
00:01:57,804 --> 00:02:02,664
The testing costs forty-four point one times more than proven alternatives

15
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:07,364
and excludes eighty-six point one percent of the patients who'll actually

16
00:02:07,364 --> 00:02:07,944
take it.

17
00:02:08,684 --> 00:02:13,124
For every one unit of harm prevented, the system creates three thousand

18
00:02:13,124 --> 00:02:15,004
and seventy through denied access.

19
00:02:16,164 --> 00:02:16,844
Here's how to fix it.

20
00:02:17,404 --> 00:02:22,044
For every one unit of harm prevented by efficacy delays, the system creates

21
00:02:22,044 --> 00:02:25,984
three thousand and seventy units of harm through denied access.

22
00:02:27,024 --> 00:02:28,644
Operational safety ratio:

23
00:02:29,084 --> 00:02:32,204
three thousand and seventy-to-one against the patient.

24
00:02:33,184 --> 00:02:37,524
In nineteen sixty-two, your Congress decided that after proving a drug won't

25
00:02:37,584 --> 00:02:42,444
kill you, sick people should wait another eight point two years before they're

26
00:02:42,444 --> 00:02:43,344
allowed to take it.

27
00:02:44,044 --> 00:02:46,164
The drug passed safety testing.

28
00:02:46,264 --> 00:02:50,044
It won't kill you, won't melt your liver, won't make your hair migrate to

29
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:50,544
your back.

30
00:02:51,264 --> 00:02:54,764
But you can't have it, because a committee needs to spend eight point two

31
00:02:54,764 --> 00:02:56,784
years making sure it works well enough.

32
00:02:57,804 --> 00:03:01,194
I asked someone why, and they said "we need to confirm efficacy."

33
00:03:01,784 --> 00:03:03,664
I said, "The patient is dying."

34
00:03:04,284 --> 00:03:07,704
They said, "Yes, but we don't know if the drug works."

35
00:03:08,044 --> 00:03:11,984
I said, "The patient could tell you, if you gave it to them."

36
00:03:12,504 --> 00:03:14,524
They said that's not how it works.

37
00:03:14,924 --> 00:03:17,404
I said, "Dying is how it works?"

38
00:03:17,904 --> 00:03:21,204
They changed the subject, which I suppose is also how it works.

39
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:25,004
You're not allowed to volunteer for the trials that would answer the question

40
00:03:25,004 --> 00:03:26,004
faster, either.

41
00:03:26,704 --> 00:03:28,714
You are, however, allowed to die.

42
00:03:28,964 --> 00:03:29,944
Nobody blocks that.

43
00:03:30,564 --> 00:03:33,524
There's no eight point two years waiting period on dying.

44
00:03:34,524 --> 00:03:38,224
On Wishonia, when we confirm something won't harm you, we let you try it.

45
00:03:38,744 --> 00:03:41,784
On Earth, you lock it in a cabinet and form a committee.

46
00:03:42,044 --> 00:03:43,364
The committee meets quarterly.

47
00:03:43,784 --> 00:03:45,784
You decompose on a different schedule.

48
00:03:46,824 --> 00:03:47,964
A Note on Blame.

49
00:03:48,644 --> 00:03:50,924
When this chapter says "the F.D.A.

50
00:03:50,984 --> 00:03:56,384
does X," read it as "the nineteen sixty-two law requires the F.D.A.

51
00:03:56,384 --> 00:03:56,884
to do X."

52
00:03:57,504 --> 00:03:58,584
Congress wrote the rules.

53
00:03:58,964 --> 00:03:59,584
The F.D.A.

54
00:03:59,644 --> 00:04:00,284
follows them.

55
00:04:00,684 --> 00:04:01,584
Blaming the F.D.A.

56
00:04:01,704 --> 00:04:05,624
is like blaming the gun instead of the person who loaded it, aimed it at

57
00:04:05,624 --> 00:04:08,944
patients, and pulled the trigger on a sixty-two-year schedule.

58
00:04:09,984 --> 00:04:11,224
"But What About Safety?"

59
00:04:11,904 --> 00:04:15,804
This is the part where humans panic, so let me be very precise about what

60
00:04:15,804 --> 00:04:18,624
this chapter is (and isn't) proposing:

61
00:04:19,464 --> 00:04:22,754
keep Phase One safety testing (it works, it caught thalidomide,

62
00:04:23,664 --> 00:04:25,284
nobody is suggesting you skip it).

63
00:04:26,024 --> 00:04:31,084
Do *radically more* efficacy testing, on *real patients*, with *transparent

64
00:04:31,084 --> 00:04:31,644
results*.

65
00:04:32,404 --> 00:04:36,404
But stop holding known-safe drugs hostage while you run the trials.

66
00:04:37,024 --> 00:04:41,124
On Wishonia, we don't have a word for "preventing someone from accessing

67
00:04:41,124 --> 00:04:44,304
a safe substance that could help them while they die."

68
00:04:44,904 --> 00:04:48,084
It would never occur to us to do it, so we never needed a word.

69
00:04:48,764 --> 00:04:50,644
You have several words for it.

70
00:04:50,744 --> 00:04:53,264
My favorite is "the approval process."

71
00:04:53,944 --> 00:04:57,204
The forty-four point one times inefficiency tax.

72
00:04:58,164 --> 00:05:01,704
Compare two real-world systems for testing drugs:

73
00:05:01,784 --> 00:05:06,184
The Oxford RECOVERY Trial tested COVID treatments on forty-eight thousand

74
00:05:06,184 --> 00:05:10,804
patients for five hundred dollars and found a life-saving treatment in three

75
00:05:10,804 --> 00:05:13,004
months, like a normal species would.

76
00:05:13,544 --> 00:05:18,604
The post-nineteen sixty-two system averages forty-one thousand dollars per

77
00:05:18,604 --> 00:05:23,704
trial and takes over a decade to approve a new drug, like humans would.

78
00:05:24,244 --> 00:05:29,684
Your efficacy testing system costs forty-four point one times more and takes

79
00:05:29,684 --> 00:05:33,324
thirty-two point eight times longer than necessary.

80
00:05:34,004 --> 00:05:36,964
I showed these numbers to a human and they said "that can't be right."

81
00:05:37,804 --> 00:05:39,724
So I showed them the sources and they said "well,

82
00:05:40,784 --> 00:05:41,464
there must be a reason."

83
00:05:42,384 --> 00:05:42,984
There is a reason.

84
00:05:43,744 --> 00:05:47,564
The reason is that your system costs forty-four point one times more and

85
00:05:47,564 --> 00:05:49,704
takes thirty-two point eight times longer.

86
00:05:50,784 --> 00:05:52,884
That's the reason and also the problem.

87
00:05:53,884 --> 00:05:55,084
They're the same thing.

88
00:05:55,884 --> 00:05:58,304
The eight point two years Efficacy Lag.

89
00:05:59,763 --> 00:06:02,444
Here's where your lifespan goes to die:

90
00:06:02,444 --> 00:06:07,384
Phase One (Safety Testing) lasts two point three years and tests if the

91
00:06:07,384 --> 00:06:08,144
drug harms people:

92
00:06:09,144 --> 00:06:14,064
death, organ damage, mutations, serious adverse reactions, all the ways

93
00:06:14,064 --> 00:06:15,524
a molecule can ruin your day.

94
00:06:16,364 --> 00:06:17,544
*This part works.

95
00:06:17,924 --> 00:06:23,744
Keep it.* Phase Two slash Three (Efficacy Testing) takes eight point two

96
00:06:23,744 --> 00:06:24,244
years.

97
00:06:24,784 --> 00:06:26,834
The drug is now *known safe*.

98
00:06:27,144 --> 00:06:29,864
But patients can't have it until the committee is satisfied.

99
00:06:30,804 --> 00:06:35,584
*This is where people die waiting for a drug that already passed every safety

100
00:06:35,744 --> 00:06:37,624
check your species invented.*

101
00:06:38,524 --> 00:06:41,824
What the nineteen sixty-two Efficacy Requirements Changed.

102
00:06:42,824 --> 00:06:47,104
Before nineteen sixty-two, one hundred and forty-four thousand physicians

103
00:06:47,104 --> 00:06:49,844
tested treatments on real patients and published results.

104
00:06:50,844 --> 00:06:54,884
Life expectancy grew three point eight two years every decade for eighty

105
00:06:54,884 --> 00:06:55,584
straight years.

106
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:57,004
Things were going well.

107
00:06:57,744 --> 00:07:00,024
Naturally, Congress intervened.

108
00:07:00,044 --> 00:07:03,104
Phase One safety testing (added in nineteen thirty-eight)

109
00:07:03,744 --> 00:07:05,144
prevented all U.S.

110
00:07:05,144 --> 00:07:07,544
thalidomide deaths while Europe had thousands.

111
00:07:08,364 --> 00:07:12,124
So in nineteen sixty-two, Congress looked at a system that was working and

112
00:07:12,124 --> 00:07:14,974
thought, "What if we made this much worse?"

113
00:07:15,784 --> 00:07:19,944
They added massive pre-approval efficacy requirements via the Kefauver Harris

114
00:07:19,944 --> 00:07:20,444
Amendment,

115
00:07:21,024 --> 00:07:23,624
blocking patient access for years during testing.

116
00:07:24,344 --> 00:07:27,904
The cost of developing a drug went from twenty-four point seven million

117
00:07:27,904 --> 00:07:33,744
dollars to two point six billion dollars, a one hundred and five times increase.

118
00:07:34,184 --> 00:07:36,714
New drug approvals dropped by seventy percent.

119
00:07:37,144 --> 00:07:41,244
Life expectancy gains slowed from three point eight two years per decade

120
00:07:41,244 --> 00:07:45,304
to one point five four, a sixty percent reduction.

121
00:07:46,004 --> 00:07:50,664
Time to approval stretched from two to three years to ten point five years.

122
00:07:51,584 --> 00:07:55,064
Everything got worse at exactly the same time.

123
00:07:55,884 --> 00:07:59,564
Every single metric, all at once, the moment the law passed.

124
00:08:00,264 --> 00:08:03,474
I'm not a statistician so I can't tell you whether that's a coincidence,

125
00:08:03,884 --> 00:08:07,224
but I did look at the graph, and it's not a coincidence.

126
00:08:07,664 --> 00:08:12,024
The one hundred and five times cost increase is rigorously documented.

127
00:08:12,164 --> 00:08:16,544
See Drug Development Cost Analysis for methodology, sensitivity analysis,

128
00:08:16,564 --> 00:08:17,604
and source data.

129
00:08:18,384 --> 00:08:19,844
The Modern Consequences.

130
00:08:20,864 --> 00:08:25,464
Even if you think historical analysis is just opinions with footnotes, the

131
00:08:25,464 --> 00:08:28,544
current system's failures are happening right now:

132
00:08:29,154 --> 00:08:30,004
One.

133
00:08:30,024 --> 00:08:31,104
A cure passes safety testing.

134
00:08:32,024 --> 00:08:32,544
Two.

135
00:08:32,744 --> 00:08:35,244
You can't take it (pending efficacy review).

136
00:08:35,704 --> 00:08:36,244
Three.

137
00:08:36,364 --> 00:08:40,804
You can't join the trial either (too sick, too old, wrong medications).

138
00:08:41,484 --> 00:08:41,984
Four.

139
00:08:42,184 --> 00:08:42,744
You die.

140
00:08:43,304 --> 00:08:43,804
Five.

141
00:08:44,024 --> 00:08:44,924
The F.D.A.

142
00:08:44,944 --> 00:08:45,824
approves the cure.

143
00:08:46,304 --> 00:08:46,804
Six.

144
00:08:46,924 --> 00:08:50,504
Pharmaceutical companies charge your widow ten thousand dollars per pill.

145
00:08:51,444 --> 00:08:54,944
I read this sequence several times because I kept thinking I'd got the order

146
00:08:54,944 --> 00:08:55,444
wrong.

147
00:08:55,804 --> 00:08:56,384
I hadn't.

148
00:08:56,724 --> 00:08:58,424
That is the correct order.

149
00:08:58,724 --> 00:09:03,984
The system works exactly like that, on purpose, and everyone involved considers

150
00:09:03,984 --> 00:09:06,684
it a success because nobody skipped a step.

151
00:09:07,784 --> 00:09:12,104
High Costs Kill Innovation, Reward Monopoly.

152
00:09:12,124 --> 00:09:13,944
Before nineteen sixty-two:

153
00:09:14,244 --> 00:09:18,884
Genius scientist invents cure, raises a few million, tests safety, gives

154
00:09:18,884 --> 00:09:19,564
it to people.

155
00:09:19,924 --> 00:09:21,684
Like a civilization that wants to survive would.

156
00:09:22,784 --> 00:09:23,504
Now:

157
00:09:23,984 --> 00:09:28,684
Genius scientist must convince one of three mega-corporations to fund trials.

158
00:09:29,344 --> 00:09:33,864
Those corporations already sell inferior drugs for the same condition, bringing

159
00:09:33,864 --> 00:09:36,104
in hundreds of millions a year per drug.

160
00:09:36,984 --> 00:09:39,404
The math for the mega-corporation:

161
00:09:39,424 --> 00:09:39,924
Option one:

162
00:09:40,404 --> 00:09:42,204
Develop the better drug Cost:

163
00:09:42,964 --> 00:09:46,684
two point six billion dollars on average to get a single drug to market.

164
00:09:47,384 --> 00:09:51,724
That figure already includes the cost of the nine candidates that fail for

165
00:09:51,724 --> 00:09:56,004
every one that succeeds, so the ten percent success rate is already priced

166
00:09:56,004 --> 00:09:56,504
in.

167
00:09:57,064 --> 00:09:58,424
Best case, the drug works:

168
00:09:58,864 --> 00:10:01,074
you now have a better drug for the same condition.

169
00:10:01,724 --> 00:10:05,164
But your old drug, which was bringing in hundreds of millions a year, is

170
00:10:05,164 --> 00:10:05,794
now obsolete.

171
00:10:06,544 --> 00:10:10,464
You spent two point six billion dollars to replace your own revenue stream.

172
00:10:11,384 --> 00:10:14,564
Every year the new drug is on the market, it's earning roughly what the

173
00:10:14,564 --> 00:10:15,974
old drug would have earned anyway,

174
00:10:16,643 --> 00:10:20,224
minus the two point six billion dollars hole you dug getting here.

175
00:10:21,184 --> 00:10:21,964
Option two:

176
00:10:22,484 --> 00:10:27,624
Buy the patent, put it on a shelf Your inferior drug keeps bringing in hundreds

177
00:10:27,624 --> 00:10:28,544
of millions a year.

178
00:10:29,164 --> 00:10:29,664
Total cost:

179
00:10:30,044 --> 00:10:33,184
whatever the patent costs, which is rounding error compared to two point

180
00:10:33,184 --> 00:10:34,244
six billion dollars.

181
00:10:35,284 --> 00:10:38,844
I asked a pharmaceutical executive which option they'd choose and they said

182
00:10:38,844 --> 00:10:40,904
"it's more nuanced than that."

183
00:10:41,664 --> 00:10:45,324
Then I asked which one they chose and they said Option two.

184
00:10:45,764 --> 00:10:47,184
So it wasn't more nuanced than that.

185
00:10:48,324 --> 00:10:52,184
The profit incentive doesn't just fail to reward better treatments.

186
00:10:52,564 --> 00:10:54,504
It actively punishes them.

187
00:10:54,684 --> 00:10:58,784
The best possible outcome of Option one is the same annual revenue you already

188
00:10:58,784 --> 00:11:02,024
had, minus two point six billion dollars.

189
00:11:02,824 --> 00:11:05,444
Curing disease is economically irrational.

190
00:11:06,184 --> 00:11:09,524
The system doesn't need a conspiracy to suppress cures.

191
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:10,984
It just needs the math.

192
00:11:11,644 --> 00:11:14,264
I keep waiting for someone to show me where the math is wrong.

193
00:11:14,944 --> 00:11:16,944
Nobody shows me where the math is wrong.

194
00:11:17,244 --> 00:11:20,244
They just look uncomfortable and say "it's complicated,"

195
00:11:21,044 --> 00:11:24,544
which I've learned is what humans say when it isn't complicated and they

196
00:11:24,544 --> 00:11:25,424
don't like the answer.

197
00:11:26,464 --> 00:11:29,004
Off-Patent Drugs and Rare Diseases:

198
00:11:29,204 --> 00:11:30,304
Mathematically Doomed.

199
00:11:31,384 --> 00:11:35,624
The nineteen sixty-two law made it mathematically impossible to cure diseases

200
00:11:35,624 --> 00:11:37,584
that aren't profitable enough:

201
00:11:38,224 --> 00:11:40,304
Ninety-five percent of diseases are rare:

202
00:11:40,784 --> 00:11:44,804
a development cost of two point six billion dollars divided by a patient

203
00:11:44,804 --> 00:11:49,884
population of about ten thousand patients equals two hundred and sixty thousand

204
00:11:49,884 --> 00:11:51,444
dollars per patient.

205
00:11:52,324 --> 00:11:57,024
No patent equals no funding because off-patent drugs can't attract billion-dollar

206
00:11:57,024 --> 00:11:57,524
investments.

207
00:11:58,444 --> 00:12:03,484
Pre-specification kills serendipity as you must predict what drug cures

208
00:12:03,484 --> 00:12:04,544
before testing.

209
00:12:05,444 --> 00:12:07,864
When something costs more, you get less of it.

210
00:12:07,964 --> 00:12:11,104
I looked this up and apparently it's the first thing they teach in economics.

211
00:12:11,604 --> 00:12:16,224
It is also, somehow, the last thing anyone considers when writing health

212
00:12:16,224 --> 00:12:16,724
policy.

213
00:12:17,544 --> 00:12:19,684
Ninety-five percent of diseases have zero treatments.

214
00:12:20,504 --> 00:12:22,104
Not because cures are impossible.

215
00:12:22,604 --> 00:12:24,544
Because cures are unprofitable.

216
00:12:25,084 --> 00:12:29,264
The best thing a disease can do for itself, career-wise, is be popular.

217
00:12:30,184 --> 00:12:32,364
The Actual Death Toll of "Drug Lag".

218
00:12:33,244 --> 00:12:36,234
Economists call it "drug lag," which is a lovely,

219
00:12:36,904 --> 00:12:41,104
clinical way of saying "people rotting to death in a queue for drugs that

220
00:12:41,104 --> 00:12:43,764
have already been confirmed not to hurt them.".

221
00:12:44,704 --> 00:12:45,404
Early estimates:

222
00:12:46,124 --> 00:12:49,924
twenty-one thousand to one hundred and twenty thousand American lives per

223
00:12:49,924 --> 00:12:50,424
decade.

224
00:12:51,324 --> 00:12:52,964
But that was just the U.S.

225
00:12:53,804 --> 00:12:58,024
A comprehensive quantitative analysis using W.H.O.

226
00:12:58,084 --> 00:13:04,304
mortality data estimates the *total* cost of the eight point two years *post-safety*

227
00:13:04,304 --> 00:13:07,524
efficacy delay (the lag *after* drugs are known safe):

228
00:13:08,364 --> 00:13:12,864
four hundred and sixteen million eventually avoidable deaths.

229
00:13:13,444 --> 00:13:16,224
Including years lived with disability:

230
00:13:16,424 --> 00:13:22,004
seven point nine four billion disability-adjusted life years, or D.A.L.Y.s,

231
00:13:22,404 --> 00:13:24,724
of healthy human life deleted.

232
00:13:25,904 --> 00:13:26,784
Economic cost:

233
00:13:27,484 --> 00:13:32,444
one point one nine quadrillion dollars (twenty twenty-four U.S.

234
00:13:32,524 --> 00:13:37,964
dollars), reflecting those seven point nine four billion D.A.L.Y.s valued

235
00:13:37,964 --> 00:13:43,504
at one hundred and fifty thousand dollars per D.A.L.Y., the standard normative

236
00:13:43,504 --> 00:13:45,724
rate used in W.H.O.

237
00:13:45,844 --> 00:13:47,464
cost-effectiveness analyses.

238
00:13:48,344 --> 00:13:51,144
Even if those death estimates are off by a factor of ten,

239
00:13:51,984 --> 00:13:54,424
that's still tens of millions of deaths.

240
00:13:54,804 --> 00:13:58,384
And the inefficiency is independently verifiable:

241
00:13:58,444 --> 00:14:03,524
the efficacy testing process costs eighty-two times more per patient and

242
00:14:03,524 --> 00:14:07,944
takes thirty-two point eight times longer than proven alternatives like

243
00:14:07,944 --> 00:14:09,444
the Oxford RECOVERY trial.

244
00:14:10,484 --> 00:14:13,944
Those numbers don't depend on mortality estimates at all.

245
00:14:15,284 --> 00:14:19,504
Here's a news story from the Non-Existent Times by No One Ever, without

246
00:14:19,504 --> 00:14:23,724
a picture of all the people who die from lack of access to life-saving treatments

247
00:14:23,724 --> 00:14:25,364
that might have been.

248
00:14:25,944 --> 00:14:30,464
You can't photograph millions of people who died from *not* receiving a

249
00:14:30,464 --> 00:14:30,964
drug.

250
00:14:31,524 --> 00:14:34,964
There's no body with a toe tag reading "cause of death:

251
00:14:35,324 --> 00:14:36,104
regulatory delay."

252
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:37,084
They die of

253
00:14:37,924 --> 00:14:38,424
cancer, heart disease,

254
00:14:39,144 --> 00:14:40,104
Alzheimer's.

255
00:14:40,164 --> 00:14:43,884
The delay that killed them is invisible, so nobody writes the headline.

256
00:14:45,324 --> 00:14:47,224
Types of Error in F.D.A.

257
00:14:47,264 --> 00:14:51,064
Approval Decision If the drug is beneficial and the F.D.A.

258
00:14:51,104 --> 00:14:53,384
allows it, that is a correct decision.

259
00:14:54,224 --> 00:14:56,424
If the drug is harmful and the F.D.A.

260
00:14:56,444 --> 00:15:00,164
allows it, victims appear on television and the regulator is fired.

261
00:15:01,044 --> 00:15:03,164
If the drug is beneficial and the F.D.A.

262
00:15:03,364 --> 00:15:07,064
does not allow it, victims die at home and nobody is fired.

263
00:15:07,964 --> 00:15:10,104
If the drug is harmful and the F.D.A.

264
00:15:10,104 --> 00:15:12,844
does not allow it, that is a correct decision.

265
00:15:13,664 --> 00:15:14,684
So the F.D.A.

266
00:15:14,904 --> 00:15:16,364
has two kinds of mistakes.

267
00:15:17,144 --> 00:15:20,034
One where they give you a bad drug and you die on television.

268
00:15:20,664 --> 00:15:24,084
And one where they don't give you a good drug and you die at home.

269
00:15:25,124 --> 00:15:29,484
They've decided the second one doesn't count, which is convenient because

270
00:15:29,484 --> 00:15:30,774
it's the one they do most.

271
00:15:31,564 --> 00:15:33,324
The most infamous case:

272
00:15:33,484 --> 00:15:34,484
beta-blockers.

273
00:15:34,524 --> 00:15:36,224
Europe used them to prevent heart attacks.

274
00:15:37,084 --> 00:15:38,004
The U.S.

275
00:15:38,024 --> 00:15:42,244
delayed for a decade, killing an estimated one hundred thousand Americans.

276
00:15:42,624 --> 00:15:45,264
More than died in Vietnam and Korea combined.

277
00:15:45,884 --> 00:15:47,104
From one drug.

278
00:15:47,184 --> 00:15:48,024
That they had.

279
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:49,424
That they knew worked.

280
00:15:49,984 --> 00:15:51,084
That they put in a drawer.

281
00:15:52,164 --> 00:15:55,624
I asked someone if there was a word for killing one hundred thousand people

282
00:15:55,624 --> 00:15:59,664
by not doing something, and they said "it depends on the context."

283
00:16:00,364 --> 00:16:04,264
I think one hundred thousand dead people is the context, but apparently

284
00:16:04,264 --> 00:16:05,584
that's not enough context.

285
00:16:06,764 --> 00:16:07,824
After nineteen sixty-two,

286
00:16:08,564 --> 00:16:09,064
U.S.

287
00:16:09,064 --> 00:16:13,044
life expectancy diverged from Switzerland's (which didn't introduce the

288
00:16:13,044 --> 00:16:13,824
same delays).

289
00:16:14,664 --> 00:16:17,104
More drug approvals in the eighties narrowed the gap.

290
00:16:17,864 --> 00:16:20,364
Fewer approvals in the nineties widened it again.

291
00:16:21,064 --> 00:16:22,754
The pattern is not subtle.

292
00:16:22,864 --> 00:16:25,304
I showed it to a child and the child understood it.

293
00:16:25,944 --> 00:16:29,234
I showed it to a policy expert and they said it was "multifactorial."

294
00:16:30,684 --> 00:16:34,964
I think "multifactorial" is what adults say when they can see the same thing

295
00:16:34,964 --> 00:16:38,344
the child can see but have reasons not to say it out loud.

296
00:16:39,344 --> 00:16:40,424
How the Incentives Work.

297
00:16:41,284 --> 00:16:41,884
F.D.A.

298
00:16:41,884 --> 00:16:42,984
Regulator Decision Tree.

299
00:16:43,944 --> 00:16:45,974
Approve drug that later shows problems.

300
00:16:46,604 --> 00:16:48,144
Congressional hearing (televised).

301
00:16:48,964 --> 00:16:49,604
"F.D.A.

302
00:16:49,684 --> 00:16:51,264
APPROVED KILLER DRUG" headlines.

303
00:16:51,784 --> 00:16:52,704
Career ends.

304
00:16:53,424 --> 00:16:54,284
Pension threatened.

305
00:16:55,184 --> 00:16:57,084
Delay drug that could save lives.

306
00:16:57,744 --> 00:16:58,764
Nothing happens.

307
00:16:58,844 --> 00:17:00,114
Nobody writes a headline.

308
00:17:00,424 --> 00:17:01,744
Promotion on schedule.

309
00:17:02,144 --> 00:17:03,384
Retire to pharma job.

310
00:17:04,364 --> 00:17:06,314
To be fair, this isn't a conspiracy.

311
00:17:06,984 --> 00:17:10,524
It's just a system where the only career-ending move is letting patients

312
00:17:10,524 --> 00:17:11,684
access treatments.

313
00:17:12,364 --> 00:17:14,744
If you approve a bad drug, C.N.N.

314
00:17:14,744 --> 00:17:15,384
says your name.

315
00:17:15,824 --> 00:17:19,524
If you delay a good drug, nobody dies on television.

316
00:17:20,064 --> 00:17:23,684
So the rational move is to delay everything, and that's what happens,

317
00:17:24,344 --> 00:17:28,104
and everyone who could object is dead, which does simplify the feedback

318
00:17:28,104 --> 00:17:30,484
process. Dr.

319
00:17:30,484 --> 00:17:31,004
Henry I.

320
00:17:31,064 --> 00:17:32,304
Miller ran the F.D.A.

321
00:17:32,544 --> 00:17:36,924
team reviewing recombinant human insulin in the early nineteen eighties.

322
00:17:37,524 --> 00:17:39,834
Mountains of evidence showed it was safe and effective.

323
00:17:40,284 --> 00:17:42,584
His supervisor refused to approve it.

324
00:17:43,124 --> 00:17:45,584
If someone died from the drug, heads would roll.

325
00:17:46,004 --> 00:17:47,964
If people died waiting for the drug?

326
00:17:48,244 --> 00:17:48,884
Nothing happens.

327
00:17:49,624 --> 00:17:52,084
Dead patients don't testify before Congress.

328
00:17:52,404 --> 00:17:52,904
I checked.

329
00:17:53,924 --> 00:17:54,724
The Math:

330
00:17:54,904 --> 00:17:58,064
Why Current Regulations Increase Total Harm.

331
00:17:58,064 --> 00:18:02,204
Even generously crediting ALL drug withdrawals to the nineteen sixty-two

332
00:18:02,204 --> 00:18:06,224
changes (ignoring that Phase One safety testing already existed),

333
00:18:06,844 --> 00:18:12,824
the prevented harm totals approximately two point five nine million disability-adjusted

334
00:18:12,824 --> 00:18:14,604
life years, or D.A.L.Y.s.

335
00:18:15,124 --> 00:18:19,024
The delay harm totals seven point nine four billion D.A.L.Y.s.

336
00:18:20,244 --> 00:18:24,824
For every one unit of harm prevented, the current system creates three thousand

337
00:18:24,824 --> 00:18:27,204
and seventy units of harm through delay.

338
00:18:27,744 --> 00:18:31,644
The safety net catches one person and drops three thousand and seventy.

339
00:18:32,324 --> 00:18:35,204
On Wishonia, we'd call that a hole, not a net.

340
00:18:36,344 --> 00:18:38,084
Clinical Trial Theater:

341
00:18:38,204 --> 00:18:42,944
Excluding eighty-six point one percent of Reality Makes Drugs More Dangerous.

342
00:18:43,344 --> 00:18:44,164
To be clear:

343
00:18:44,504 --> 00:18:48,083
Phase One safety testing should exclude vulnerable populations.

344
00:18:48,764 --> 00:18:51,684
You don't give an untested molecule to a pregnant woman.

345
00:18:52,224 --> 00:18:57,264
But once a drug clears safety, the efficacy trials that follow *also* exclude

346
00:18:57,264 --> 00:18:58,004
those populations,

347
00:18:58,624 --> 00:19:02,063
which means nobody learns whether the drug works for the people who will

348
00:19:02,063 --> 00:19:05,364
actually take it, or what interactions to expect.

349
00:19:06,144 --> 00:19:09,884
Then the drug is approved for everyone, and the post-market surveillance

350
00:19:09,884 --> 00:19:15,184
system (the Adverse Event Reporting System, or F.A.E.R.S.)

351
00:19:15,184 --> 00:19:17,804
catches less than ten percent of adverse events.

352
00:19:18,304 --> 00:19:22,084
So the exclusions create a data gap, and nothing ever fills it.

353
00:19:22,924 --> 00:19:23,984
The F.D.A.

354
00:19:23,984 --> 00:19:25,504
requires rigorous safety trials.

355
00:19:25,864 --> 00:19:26,364
Good.

356
00:19:26,604 --> 00:19:30,884
Then it runs efficacy trials on people who aren't sick, aren't old, aren't

357
00:19:30,884 --> 00:19:33,384
on other drugs, and aren't pregnant.

358
00:19:33,404 --> 00:19:34,954
I read this three times.

359
00:19:35,604 --> 00:19:39,784
They test whether drugs work on people who don't need the drugs, to predict

360
00:19:39,784 --> 00:19:43,544
whether they'll work for people who do need the drugs, who are different

361
00:19:43,544 --> 00:19:46,824
people, with different bodies, taking different medications.

362
00:19:47,304 --> 00:19:50,804
Then they act surprised when the second group has a reaction.

363
00:19:51,324 --> 00:19:55,144
I would call this stupid but I think it might actually be something worse

364
00:19:55,144 --> 00:19:56,124
than stupid.

365
00:19:56,764 --> 00:19:59,594
Stupid doesn't usually have a peer-review process.

366
00:20:00,204 --> 00:20:03,084
Trials under the current system exclude:

367
00:20:03,164 --> 00:20:04,824
Patients over sixty-five:

368
00:20:04,904 --> 00:20:09,464
Most people who actually take medications (excluded due to "comorbidities").

369
00:20:10,024 --> 00:20:11,244
Patients under eighteen:

370
00:20:11,764 --> 00:20:14,284
All children (metabolism differs from adults).

371
00:20:14,744 --> 00:20:15,624
Pregnant women:

372
00:20:15,724 --> 00:20:19,924
Excluded entirely (then drugs prescribed during pregnancy anyway).

373
00:20:20,424 --> 00:20:22,244
Anyone with comorbidities:

374
00:20:22,304 --> 00:20:25,884
The sickest patients most likely to have adverse reactions.

375
00:20:26,464 --> 00:20:28,724
Anyone on other medications:

376
00:20:28,744 --> 00:20:31,644
Everyone elderly (can't detect drug interactions).

377
00:20:32,204 --> 00:20:33,984
Anyone too far from trial sites:

378
00:20:34,544 --> 00:20:35,674
Poor and rural populations.

379
00:20:36,544 --> 00:20:40,944
It's like testing whether a car is safe by driving it very slowly into a

380
00:20:40,944 --> 00:20:44,494
nice cushion, and then selling it to people who drive into walls.

381
00:20:44,924 --> 00:20:48,404
And when they die you say "well, it was safe when WE tried it."

382
00:20:48,784 --> 00:20:49,584
Which is true.

383
00:20:49,644 --> 00:20:50,184
It was.

384
00:20:50,864 --> 00:20:51,364
Result:

385
00:20:51,784 --> 00:20:56,484
In antidepressant trials alone, eighty-six point one percent of real patients

386
00:20:56,484 --> 00:20:57,674
are excluded.

387
00:20:58,164 --> 00:21:00,704
The drugs are tested on the healthiest people alive,

388
00:21:01,304 --> 00:21:05,604
declared "safe and effective," then handed to everyone the trial specifically

389
00:21:05,604 --> 00:21:06,504
avoided.

390
00:21:07,284 --> 00:21:10,924
Nobody knows whether the drug works for those populations, what the interactions

391
00:21:10,924 --> 00:21:14,764
are, or what the real adverse event profile looks like.

392
00:21:15,344 --> 00:21:19,144
This is how Vioxx, Fen-Phen, and Bextra all got approved,

393
00:21:19,864 --> 00:21:23,984
celebrated, prescribed to millions, and then withdrawn after killing people

394
00:21:23,984 --> 00:21:27,264
whose demographics the trials had carefully excluded.

395
00:21:27,984 --> 00:21:31,584
The eight point two years delay didn't make these drugs safer.

396
00:21:32,004 --> 00:21:36,704
It made them seem safer by hiding the danger behind an exclusion list.

397
00:21:37,264 --> 00:21:42,004
Testing drugs only on unrepresentative volunteers to prove they work is

398
00:21:42,004 --> 00:21:44,584
like testing parachutes only on the ground.

399
00:21:44,984 --> 00:21:47,224
The parachute worked perfectly, by the way.

400
00:21:47,544 --> 00:21:49,084
It just wasn't falling at the time.

401
00:21:50,104 --> 00:21:52,044
No Long-Term Outcome Data.

402
00:21:52,064 --> 00:21:54,524
Data collection can be as short as several months.

403
00:21:55,084 --> 00:21:57,004
You take the drug for forty years.

404
00:21:57,704 --> 00:22:00,944
The gap between these two numbers is where side effects live.

405
00:22:01,564 --> 00:22:02,384
Nobody checks.

406
00:22:02,644 --> 00:22:04,964
It's like reviewing a marriage based on the wedding.

407
00:22:05,604 --> 00:22:09,124
Pre-Specification Requirements Kill Innovation.

408
00:22:09,124 --> 00:22:13,444
The regulations require drug developers to predict exactly what a treatment

409
00:22:13,444 --> 00:22:16,104
will cure before testing it on humans.

410
00:22:16,644 --> 00:22:20,064
You must know the answer before you're allowed to ask the question.

411
00:22:20,784 --> 00:22:24,684
I asked if this was how science works and they said "it's how regulatory

412
00:22:24,684 --> 00:22:29,324
science works," which I think means "no, but we gave it the same name.".

413
00:22:30,084 --> 00:22:34,964
In two thousand and seven, Dendreon showed that its immunotherapy drug Provenge

414
00:22:34,964 --> 00:22:38,364
significantly reduced deaths from prostate cancer.

415
00:22:38,924 --> 00:22:39,644
The F.D.A.

416
00:22:39,884 --> 00:22:42,004
advisory committee agreed it worked.

417
00:22:42,024 --> 00:22:43,644
Then the F.D.A.

418
00:22:43,724 --> 00:22:44,224
rejected it anyway.

419
00:22:45,324 --> 00:22:46,824
Not because it didn't save lives.

420
00:22:47,284 --> 00:22:52,224
Because Dendreon filled out the wrong form about which lives it was planning

421
00:22:52,224 --> 00:22:52,784
to save.

422
00:22:53,564 --> 00:22:55,744
"People stopped dying" wasn't good enough.

423
00:22:56,344 --> 00:23:00,304
The paperwork predicting that people would stop dying wasn't filed in the

424
00:23:00,304 --> 00:23:01,044
right order.

425
00:23:01,584 --> 00:23:04,424
Three more years and another trial were required.

426
00:23:04,884 --> 00:23:08,624
During those three years, people who could have stopped dying continued

427
00:23:08,624 --> 00:23:11,424
dying, but at least the forms were correct.

428
00:23:12,244 --> 00:23:14,204
On Wishonia, we have a saying:

429
00:23:14,224 --> 00:23:16,164
"The gravestone was filed on time."

430
00:23:16,644 --> 00:23:21,144
It means someone prioritized procedure over the thing the procedure was

431
00:23:21,144 --> 00:23:22,224
supposed to protect.

432
00:23:22,804 --> 00:23:27,104
We retired the saying because it kept applying to too many situations.

433
00:23:27,604 --> 00:23:28,764
You could use it daily.

434
00:23:29,364 --> 00:23:34,524
Due to these additional costs, Dendreon filed for chapter eleven bankruptcy.

435
00:23:35,104 --> 00:23:39,824
So the approval process killed the patients, then killed the company trying

436
00:23:39,824 --> 00:23:40,564
to save them.

437
00:23:41,204 --> 00:23:42,324
You have a phrase for this:

438
00:23:42,684 --> 00:23:44,364
"killing two birds with one stone."

439
00:23:44,824 --> 00:23:48,824
Although in this case the stone was paperwork and there were considerably

440
00:23:48,824 --> 00:23:49,924
more than two birds.

441
00:23:50,504 --> 00:23:53,944
But you can't count the dead birds who would have been cured by a company

442
00:23:53,944 --> 00:23:54,864
you bankrupted.

443
00:23:55,384 --> 00:23:57,724
The Blinding Catch-22:

444
00:23:57,804 --> 00:24:00,584
How Knowing a Drug Works Proves It Doesn't.

445
00:24:01,324 --> 00:24:02,324
M.D.M.A.

446
00:24:02,324 --> 00:24:04,084
was synthesized in nineteen twelve.

447
00:24:04,624 --> 00:24:08,584
By the nineteen seventies, therapists were using it to treat trauma, and

448
00:24:08,584 --> 00:24:13,244
an estimated half a million doses were administered in therapeutic settings.

449
00:24:13,324 --> 00:24:15,924
In nineteen eighty-five, the government scheduled it.

450
00:24:16,464 --> 00:24:21,204
In nineteen eighty-six, Rick Doblin founded the Multidisciplinary Association

451
00:24:21,204 --> 00:24:26,044
for Psychedelic Studies, or M.A.P.S., to get it approved for P.T.S.D.

452
00:24:26,684 --> 00:24:31,304
Thirty-eight years and over one hundred and forty million dollars in philanthropic

453
00:24:31,424 --> 00:24:35,624
funding later, they ran two successful Phase three trials.

454
00:24:36,184 --> 00:24:40,864
Sixty-seven percent of participants no longer met the diagnostic criteria

455
00:24:40,864 --> 00:24:42,064
for P.T.S.D.

456
00:24:42,464 --> 00:24:43,944
The drug worked.

457
00:24:43,944 --> 00:24:46,604
Veterans with treatment-resistant P.T.S.D.

458
00:24:46,604 --> 00:24:47,564
got better.

459
00:24:47,584 --> 00:24:51,184
The F.D.A.'s own advisory committee reviewed the data.

460
00:24:51,184 --> 00:24:54,614
They voted nine to two that it wasn't effective.

461
00:24:54,964 --> 00:24:55,584
The problem:

462
00:24:56,224 --> 00:25:00,384
patients could tell they'd taken M.D.M.A., because M.D.M.A.

463
00:25:00,384 --> 00:25:03,334
makes you feel things, which is how it treats P.T.S.D.,

464
00:25:04,184 --> 00:25:05,204
which is the point.

465
00:25:05,724 --> 00:25:09,624
About ninety percent of participants in the drug group correctly guessed

466
00:25:09,624 --> 00:25:11,164
they weren't on placebo.

467
00:25:11,724 --> 00:25:12,264
The F.D.A.

468
00:25:12,444 --> 00:25:17,004
called this "functional unblinding" and said it invalidated the results.

469
00:25:17,564 --> 00:25:19,664
I want to make sure I understand the logic.

470
00:25:20,164 --> 00:25:22,564
The drug works by making you feel profoundly different.

471
00:25:23,424 --> 00:25:24,104
The F.D.A.

472
00:25:24,364 --> 00:25:27,284
requires that you not know whether you feel profoundly different.

473
00:25:27,964 --> 00:25:31,844
If you notice that you feel profoundly different, the trial fails, because

474
00:25:31,844 --> 00:25:33,504
you weren't supposed to notice.

475
00:25:34,144 --> 00:25:38,144
The drug's mechanism of action is, itself, a protocol violation.

476
00:25:39,064 --> 00:25:40,854
This is not a fixable design problem.

477
00:25:41,464 --> 00:25:45,584
You cannot double-blind a drug whose therapeutic effect is that the patient

478
00:25:45,584 --> 00:25:46,664
feels it working.

479
00:25:47,544 --> 00:25:48,164
The F.D.A.

480
00:25:48,164 --> 00:25:48,664
knows this.

481
00:25:49,244 --> 00:25:50,724
They granted M.D.M.A.

482
00:25:50,724 --> 00:25:54,984
"Breakthrough Therapy Designation" in twenty seventeen, signaling that yes,

483
00:25:55,264 --> 00:25:56,044
this looks promising,

484
00:25:56,724 --> 00:26:00,044
please spend another seven years and tens of millions of dollars on Phase

485
00:26:00,044 --> 00:26:00,544
three trials.

486
00:26:01,464 --> 00:26:06,484
Then they rejected it for a property of the molecule that was evident before

487
00:26:06,484 --> 00:26:07,204
the trials began.

488
00:26:08,524 --> 00:26:12,404
On Wishonia, if you tell someone to build a house and then condemn it for

489
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:14,784
having walls, you owe them a house.

490
00:26:15,344 --> 00:26:16,404
Here, you owe them nothing.

491
00:26:17,064 --> 00:26:18,784
The veterans kept their P.T.S.D.

492
00:26:19,064 --> 00:26:19,704
The F.D.A.

493
00:26:19,764 --> 00:26:20,584
kept its process.

494
00:26:20,964 --> 00:26:24,264
Everyone kept exactly what they had, which was the problem in the first

495
00:26:24,264 --> 00:26:24,764
place.

496
00:26:25,564 --> 00:26:29,884
Meanwhile, approximately forty-nine thousand Americans kill themselves every

497
00:26:29,884 --> 00:26:30,384
year,

498
00:26:31,004 --> 00:26:34,504
including six thousand four hundred veterans at twice the civilian rate.

499
00:26:35,164 --> 00:26:37,804
About thirteen million Americans have P.T.S.D.

500
00:26:37,824 --> 00:26:40,404
in any given year, and P.T.S.D.

501
00:26:40,404 --> 00:26:42,144
nearly quadruples your suicide risk.

502
00:26:43,304 --> 00:26:47,484
M.D.M.A.-assisted therapy produced a sixty-seven percent remission rate

503
00:26:47,484 --> 00:26:49,584
versus thirty-two percent for standard care.

504
00:26:50,224 --> 00:26:52,824
Even conservatively, if half of P.T.S.D.

505
00:26:53,124 --> 00:26:56,404
